Figure 2 shows an example of the visualization of the localization result used for navigation guidance. The scenario is that the mobile computer user is working in a large industrial building and the user is surrounded by huge containers, pipes, and other equipments. A floor-map of the working site is displayed in the main window of the application. There is a red dot showing the position of the user. A green line is shown on the floor-map as a navigation guidance.

We augment the real-time video with text and virtual objects to provide the mobile computer user with more information. For example, we can carpet the floor in the image with the floor map and put arrows on the floor as a navigation guidance, as shown in Figure 2 .

Figure 3 shows another case when the user points the camera to an equipment, the system automatically switches the display from the floor-map to a industrial drawing of the equipment of interest. There is a web browser automatically connecting the user to the corresponding data resource.
